WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.990 --> 00:01:07.030 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  lately  i've been alone  [Music]  alone with my thoughts  alone with my fears  just  alone  the desert can be beautiful like that  there are roads that lead to nowhere and  places you can go where you won't see  another soul  dave leads in tonight and night leads in  today  until time itself just  kind of fades away  then  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  i spent most of april and nearly all of  may alone  reading walking writing  i just kind of hid away from the world  trying to make sense of things  i had a hard time motivating myself to  do anything work related much less to  create  i sat in silence and thought a lot about  the life i was living  i felt  whatever it was i needed to feel and did  my best to avoid distraction  [Music]  it was difficult  [Music]  but also healing  and beautiful  [Music]  [Music]  it's always there  watching  steadfast  knowing us in our light and dark moments  changing forever  just as we do  [Music]  every day it's a different version of  itself  sometimes weak  sometimes strong and full of light  the moon knows what it means to be human  uncertain  alone  cratered by imperfection  [Music]  [Applause]  thank you to moon for sponsoring this  video  some of you might have noticed that my  fan doesn't have a roof rack so when  moon offered to send me their moon shade  awning i was surprised to learn that it  didn't require roof rack or any kind of  permanent attachment  moonshade is a portable awning that can  easily mount to all kinds of rigs it  attaches pretty easily using a variety  of methods there are magnets or suction  cups and they work great with rv schooly  truck camper van you name it it takes  about five minutes to set up packs down  to roughly the size of a yoga mat and  weighs just eight pounds also side note  the mount comes in really handy for  hanging my shower bag as well this is  where i store the moon awning and it  fits perfectly right here in the  passenger side it's in there nice and  snug and i use the magnetic anchors to  hold it in place adding a moon shade to  my rake has improved my home in a few  ways extra living space a solution for  hanging my shower and an awning to  escape the summer heat which makes it  pretty perfect for road life  check out the link in my caption below  to pick up your own moon shade and  thanks again to moon for sponsoring this  video  [Music]  somewhere in there a two-week pet sit in  park city utah became available and the  thought of snow-capped mountains and  cooler weather sounded like heaven  and it was  [Music]  i wasn't alone for this set which was  nice because it also happened to be my  birthday  i turned 37  i think if you would have told 17 year  old me that when i turned 37 i would be  living in my car  alone working as a self-employed artist  i think i would have burst into tears  obviously there's more to it but on  paper those are the facts  17 year old me would have expected 37  year old me to have her life together to  be living overseas climbing the  corporate ladder living in a big  beautiful modern home married with a dog  and 2.5 kids  that wasn't exactly my idea of happiness  but i believed it was what i was  supposed to want  the truth is i have actually experienced  most of those things in the past 20  years and a hell of a lot more  but those things don't guarantee  happiness  happiness is an inside job as they say  still i'm so grateful for all of it  because it has all led  to here  the great wide empty  miles and miles of open road  freedom golden light and starry nights  a subtle yet steady shift away from  society and all the expectations that  come with it  [Music]  i know it won't last forever  but for now  i'm leaning in  to the solitude  the  unknown and everything in between  as i head into my fifth year of living  full-time on the road i've learned a few  things  actually i could probably create a whole  video on what i've learned but if i were  to summarize it would be this  the road has taught me to notice rather  than to search  to appreciate rather than to analyze  to accept that i'm on a journey to  nowhere and  everywhere all at once  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  for now these roads to nowhere are my  home  these wild spaces  are my classroom  and every person challenge and joy i  find along the way  is my teacher  one way or another  so here's to four years on the road  37 years on this earth  and everything new that lies ahead  and here's to you for being here  thank you  and i'll see you soon

